WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.920
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Monday, November 23.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.550
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in transhumanism.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.930
Still working!

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.620
The week's best: a woman in Boston has lived a year with a pig kidney.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.510
And OpenAI's chief scientist wants AI lab

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.050
s to agree on limits they won't cross yet.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.750
And Anthropic's Riemann mathematician is back,

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.440
now claiming an AI-aided fluid-flow proof.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.760
A startup says AI agents designed a new processor from scratch,

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.400
though no chip exists yet.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.520
OpenAI built a drug-design exam for AI; its best model scored about 85%.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.580
And why is the brain wired crosswise?

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:58.770
A new theory traces it to ancient fish eyes.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.020
On to longevity.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:06.080
Britons born under sugar rationing look up to 5 months younger in blood tests.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.170
And with calories matched,

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:14.160
an ultraprocessed meal still sparked a bigger insulin surge in 32 volunteers.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.280
In mice, a Berkeley compound burned fat but spared muscle,

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.500
lifting energy use up to 18%.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.780
And in 100 people with knee arthritis,

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.390
adding core workouts helped more than knee exercises alone.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.100
On to wellbeing.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:37.460
48 therapists tried fast breathing; their bliss scores resembled moderate psychedelic doses.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.260
Meanwhile, in 36 adults,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.480
low-dose THC made people feel high but didn't ease a stressful memory.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.990
Now, the catch. In New Zealand,

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:52.310
ChatGPT's Mandarin versions of mental-health checklists changed from user to user.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.540
And big US banks now say: let an AI agent into your account at your own risk.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.970
On the frontier, a Sydney astronomer may have redrawn part of our galaxy's map.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.020
In Japan, a physicist built a mock black hole from logic gates,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.260
then made it leak.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.660
And a reusable space factory for growing dr

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.450
ug crystals aims to be flight-ready by 2030.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.530
One year, one pig kidney, no dialysis.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.190
Every extra year is the point. Still working!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.950
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.350
Go build the future. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
